<title>UK: Reuters 4th Ex-UK-Americas air cargo market report.</title>
<headline>Reuters 4th Ex-UK-Americas air cargo market report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are the current average ex-UK air cargo rates to the United States per kg for a 100 kg shipment, with a volume-to-weight ratio of six-to-one.</p>
<p>		   March 27	  March 14</p>
<p>		  UNITED STATES</p>
<p> LON-CHI	 0.74		  0.77</p>
<p> LON-JFK	 0.62		  0.64</p>
<p> LON-LAX	 0.80		  0.82</p>
<p>.LON-MIA	 0.63		  N.A.</p>
<p>		  LATIN AMERICA</p>
<p> LON-SAO	1.90		   2.08</p>
<p> LON-BUE	2.02		   2.21</p>
<p> LON-SCL	1.80		   N.A.</p>
<p>*The rates quoted in this report were obtained by Reuters journalists on a confidential basis from a range of airlines, large forwarders and smaller air cargo agents at the three main London airports.</p>
<p>*All prices are quoted in sterling.</p>
<p>*The tariffs represent average rates calculated from a range of prices and are indicative of current market activity.</p>
</text>
